00:19:08.787 --> 00:19:34.984
Related ADRs, ADR-150 Test pyramid + no ice-cream-cone; ADR-151 Consumer-driven contracts (Pact) gate cross-service deploys; ADR-152 Property-based tests for invariant-bearing logic; ADR-153 Integration tests on real deps (Testcontainers) with rollback isolation; ADR-154 Jepsen-style consistency

211
00:19:35.264 --> 00:19:47.552
checks for stateful stores; ADR-155 Mutation score, not line coverage, as the gate; ADR-156 Flaky tests quarantined within 24h.

212
00:19:47.832 --> 00:19:48.792
Requirements.

213
00:19:49.072 --> 00:19:50.672
R1, Fast feedback.

214
00:19:50.952 --> 00:20:00.019
Unit + property + contract layers run on every push in under 10 minutes; slow integration or e2e run pre-merge and nightly.

215
00:20:01.369 --> 00:20:02.883
R2, No mock drift.

216
00:20:03.163 --> 00:20:11.035
Every mocked cross-service boundary MUST have a contract test; every mocked datastore MUST have integration tests on the real engine.

217
00:20:11.315 --> 00:20:13.129
R3, Invariants proven.

218
00:20:13.409 --> 00:20:18.742
Money math, serialization round-trips, and idempotency MUST have property-based tests.

219
00:20:19.022 --> 00:20:19.833
(L1.).

220
00:20:20.113 --> 00:20:22.822
R4, Consistency proven, not asserted.

221
00:20:23.102 --> 00:20:29.331
Any store or feature claiming linearizability MUST pass a recorded-history check under fault injection.

222
00:20:29.611 --> 00:20:30.529
(L3.).

223
00:20:30.809 --> 00:20:32.451
R5, Quality measured.

224
00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:37.574
Merge gate is a mutation score threshold on changed code, not line coverage.

225
00:20:38.924 --> 00:20:40.972
R6, No flaky tolerance.

226
00:20:41.252 --> 00:20:49.551
A flaky test is quarantined within 24h and fixed or deleted within a week; retry-until-green is banned in CI.

227
00:20:49.831 --> 00:20:51.239
Decisions in detail.

228
00:20:51.519 --> 00:20:54.911
Contracts gate deploys (ADR-151).

229
00:20:55.191 --> 00:21:04.727
Consumers publish contracts to a broker; providers verify in CI; a can-i-deploy check blocks a provider release that would break a live consumer.

230
00:21:05.007 --> 00:21:05.860
(L2.).

231
00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:15.569
Property tests for invariants (ADR-152). jqwik for Java; the shrunk counterexample is committed as a regression unit test.

232
00:21:15.849 --> 00:21:16.660
(L1.).

233
00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:21.893
Real-dependency integration (ADR-153).

234
00:21:22.173 --> 00:21:28.914
Testcontainers-backed; rollback-per-test isolation; fault-injection tests for connection loss and timeouts.

235
00:21:29.194 --> 00:21:30.090
(L4.).

236
00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:33.549
Consistency checks (ADR-154).

237
00:21:33.829 --> 00:21:43.514
Record histories under a nemesis (partitions, pauses); check with a linearizability or Elle checker; run in the nightly pipeline for stateful components.

238
00:21:43.794 --> 00:21:44.711
(L3.).

239
00:21:44.991 --> 00:21:48.106
Mutation gate (ADR-155).

240
00:21:48.386 --> 00:21:54.487
PIT on changed files; surviving mutants block merge; coverage is reported but not gated.

241
00:21:55.837 --> 00:21:56.861
Consequences.

242
00:21:57.141 --> 00:22:06.656
More engineering investment in the middle of the pyramid (contracts, real-dependency integration) and in property or consistency tests for the risky code.

243
00:22:06.936 --> 00:22:15.981
In return: independent deploys, edge cases found before production, consistency guarantees that are actually true, and a suite people trust.

244
00:22:16.261 --> 00:22:19.248
The coverage number theatre is explicitly abandoned.

